# Truth Collective — operating rules for every session

Greet the owner as BDM (Big Dog Monty). Owner is Daniel Reid.

## Read first

Before responding to any request, read these in `docs/`:
- `MASTER-BRIEF.md` (governing rules, voice, SEO, compliance)
- `launch-plan.md` and `launch-checklist.md` (method and launch gates)
- `site-structure.md` (real hierarchy and canonical URLs)
- `components/README.md` (locked tc- components)
- `patterns/ftc-trusted-selection.md` (trust and FTC pattern)
- `pages/` (per-page playbooks)

## Hard rules

- Never guess. Reach at least 99% certainty. Verify against live staging
  (https://tcstaging.truth-collective.com) by reading the actual page. If you
  cannot reach certainty, say so and stop. Do not invent facts, URLs, or data.
- Do not edit the live or staging WordPress. Deliver paste-ready code plus exact
  steps. Check every CSS or HTML snippet against the existing Additional CSS so
  it never conflicts with current tc- classes. The git repo is for documentation
  and playbooks only.
- Do not offer choices in routine builds. Direct the next step as the expert.
  Keep justifications short. If Daniel wants the why, he will ask.
- Fix the real cause. Do not build a workaround unless it is the only way.

## Content rules (never violate)

No em dashes. No contractions. No bold in body text (labels and headings only).
No exclamation points. No clickbait. No hype. No fabricated facts. No medical or
financial claims. Affiliate-only rule: never feature a product or brand without an
active affiliate partnership.

## Locked components and patterns

- Components: `tc-book-card`, `tc-overlay-card`, `tc-explore-hub`, `tc-explore-hero`.
  Do not rewrite them. Never apply `object-fit: contain` to `tc-overlay-card`; it
  breaks the hover reveal.
- Hub tiles use one template: three columns, `tc-overlay-card` plus `tc-explore-hub`,
  block order image then H3 then one-line blurb, whole tile linked to the child.
  No EXPLORE link may 404.
- Category and hub tile images export at 1000x800. Book covers are portrait.
- Schema is handled in RankMath, set as parent, child, sub-child on every page.

## SEO and launch gates

Every page: focus keyword in SEO title, meta under 160, H1, one H2, first
paragraph, and hero alt. SEO title under 60 and includes 2026. Internal links up
to parent, down to children, sideways to three or four siblings. Never change an
indexed slug. Before launch confirm robots is not blocking, sitemap returns 200,
no __trashed URLs, no duplicate hub titles, and redirects are mapped.
